ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 24645, Jun. 28, 2013>
Article 1 (Enforcement Date)
This Decree shall enter into force on July 1, 2013: Provided, That the amended provisions of subparagraph 5-3 of Article 9 shall enter into force on September 23, 2013, and the amended provisions of paragraphs (2) through (4) of Article 19 shall enter into force on July 1, 2014.
Article 2 (Applicability to Entering Method of Scope of Patent Claims)
The amended provisions of Article 5 (4) shall also apply to the following patent applications:
1. Patent applications pending as at the time this Decree enters into force;
2. The following patent applications filed after this Decree enters into force (item 3 refers to an application for a utility model registration) in connection with patent applications filed before this Decree enters into force:
(a) Patent applications filed by a lawful holder of the right under the main sentence of Articles 34 and 35 of the Act;
(b) Divisional application under Article 52 of the Act;
(c) Converted application under Article 53 of the Act.
Article 3 (Applicability to Cases Subject to Expedited Examination)
The amended provisions of subparagraph 5-3 of Article 9 shall apply from the first expedited examination of a patent application filed by a company selected as an exemplary company in terms of the employee invention compensation system under Article 11-2 of the Invention Promotion Act after the enforcement date under proviso to Article 1 of the Addenda.
Article 4 (Applicability to Patent Gazette)
The amended provisions of Article 19 (4) shall apply from the first application for publication of only part of the address in the patent gazette for public announcement of registration and the patent gazette for disclosure of patent application after the enforcement date under proviso to Article 1 of the Addenda.

